<title>USA: Seagate sets $70 mln Philippine expansion.</title>
<headline>Seagate sets $70 mln Philippine expansion.</headline>
<dateline>SCOTTS VALLEY, Calif. 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seagate Technology Inc said Tuesday it will spend an additional $70 million to expand its computer disk drive recording head manufacturing facility in the Philippines.</p>
<p>Construction of a 350,000-square-foot facility in the province of Cebu will begin in the 1997 first quarter, it said. Production should begin in early 1998.</p>
<p>At full capacity the plant could produce 80 million head gimbal assemblies a year, it said.</p>
<p>Seagate invested about $300 million in its recording head business in 1996 and expects to spend another $300 million in 1997, it said.</p>
</text>
